  "captured_at": "2026-11-04",
  "blocks": [
    {
      "text": "This article provides information for managing Zscaler Private Access (ZPA) Microtenants using APIs. All APIs are rate limited. To learn more, see Understanding Rate Limiting."
    },
    {
      "text": "The following conditions apply when passing microtenantId, the unique identifier of the Microtenant, in a request:"
    },
    {
      "item": "If you are within a Microtenant, you must pass the microtenantId field when making an API call to retrieve data from that Microtenant. The microtenantId can be obtained in the API Keys page, or can be obtained programmatically using the ZPA cloud service API. Access to certain operations are limited when you are within a Microtenant.",
      "depth": 0
    },
    {
      "item": "If you are within the Default Microtenant, pass microtenantId as 0 when making requests to retrieve data from the Default Microtenant.",
      "depth": 0
    },
    {
      "item": "When making requests using inheritable resources, you can pass microtenantId as null to retrieve data from all Microtenants associated with the tenant. Click here to see a list of inheritable resources.",
      "depth": 0
    },
